  <div class="prose-hgg mt-10">
    <h2>How to use these guides</h2>
    <p><strong>Start with the load-based guide.</strong> Gather exact appliance nameplates and manuals, list which loads may run together, and use the <a href="/sizing/appliance-wattage-chart/">appliance wattage reference</a> only as a generic manufacturer-published estimate when exact data is unavailable. Then ask a qualified local professional to assess the generator, fuel supply, transfer equipment, site conditions, and local requirements.</p>
    <p>These pages do not provide a calculator, estimator, universal multiplier, floor-area rule, or purchase recommendation. A generator’s selected rating and backed-up-load plan influence the equipment and installation scope, but only a property-specific assessment can determine whether a proposed design fits.</p>
